{"seq":14,"trial_id":"v02-heldout-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-mu-v02-heldout/ms-06-phl-tickets/r1","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T04:42:02.425Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"c67f0a7216d47281c4a28a7fcbd69501af489c63d56be90e3fff0c33c87f50d1","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"@Bettina Kroll, here's the list for Kwame's review. I left out Pellow Home Living. Tickets and requests came from #coastal-team, #coastal-random, and Moss's Coastal notes.\n\n**Pellucid Harbor Logistics (PHL)**\n- **#4419** (open): the `Yard_Dwell_Summary` report times out when filtered by container length. *Source: Moss's Coastal cheat sheet.*\n- **PD-8841**: double-booked gates and chassis pool holds at Gate 4B, from the December cutover recap. *Source: your cutover recap note.*\n- **Conflict to check:** Moss's 11/2 digest also lists #4419, but attributes it to Puget Sound Operations (barge slip 7 schedule sync). I can't tell from the notes which account it belongs to, so it's worth confirming before the review.\n\n**Driftmoor Marine Freight (DMF)**\n- **Feature request #882**: a bulk-clear button for departed barges. *Source: Moss's cheat sheet.*\n- **Tide-table import macro failure on Terminal B.** Engineering provided a manual CSV patch for the night dispatcher. No ticket number is recorded. *Source: Moss's cheat sheet.*\n- **Manifest CSV patch** requested before the 06:00 shift. No ticket number is recorded. *Source: Moss's 11/2 digest.*\n\nI didn't include PD-4827 (Corinne Ashdown's Pemberline Dock admin access, Saltmarsh Provisions) or #8812 (the Door 4B scanner, Pellow Home Living). Neither is PHL or DMF."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
